# .quartoignore -- directories Quarto must not walk when discovering project inputs.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Before rendering anything, Quarto enumerates the project directory to find
# its inputs. It skips names beginning with "_" or ".", so _rendered/, _BackUp/, _Commons/, _Tests/
# and .quarto/ cost nothing. Everything else at the root is walked in full -- including a package
# library, four Python virtual environments and an output tree holding the parsed corpus. That walk
# is hundreds of thousands of stat calls before a single line of R runs, and it is the reason a
# render can sit for a minute with no output at all.
#
# The `render:` list in _quarto.yml does NOT prevent this. That list decides which discovered inputs
# are rendered; the discovery happens first and walks everything either way.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's. Add a line here whenever a large directory appears at the root.

# Package library. Several hundred packages, tens of thousands of files, no .qmd anywhere in it.
renv/

# Python. Each of these carries a .venv/ once it has been set up, and a venv is the single largest
# file count in the repository after the corpus.
contracts-classify/
contracts-extract/
contracts-lexnlp/
contracts-spacy/
_contracts-engine/
_contracts-extract/

# Derived data. The EDGAR mirror, the staged parquet and the DuckDB stores. Regenerated by the
# pipeline, shipped via the DOI archive, and never an input to a render.
2_output/
0_data/
0_sample/
0_scratch/
_BackUps

# The public site is a SECOND Quarto project with its own configuration and its own output
# directory. It is built by 3_site/_build.R, never by a render at this root.
3_site/
docs/

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
